# Port Daddy — Environment Variables
# Copy to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are used by fleet agents to call AI backends.
# The daemon itself does not need API keys.

# Required for fleet agents using Claude backend
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional: allow the daemon's semantic resolver to download its embedding
# model (Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2) from huggingface.co when it is not cached
# locally. Default is OFF: no opt-in means no network fetch — the resolver
# serves lexical/BM25 results labeled degraded until the model is prefetched
# (scripts/prefetch-embedding-model.ts) or this is set. TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1
# always wins over this opt-in.
# PORT_DADDY_ALLOW_MODEL_DOWNLOAD=1

# Optional: for fleet agents using other backends
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434

# Optional developer overrides for the pd-console Voyage Timeline companion.
# Pin a built executable directly, or point at the standalone proto crate whose
# target/{release,debug} outputs should be searched.
# PD_TIMELINE_PROTO_BIN=/absolute/path/to/pd-timeline-proto
# PD_TIMELINE_PROTO_DIR=/absolute/path/to/core/pd-timeline-proto

# ── The Steward's seat (ADR-0109) — LOCAL COPIES of Worker secrets ───────────
#
# READ THIS FIRST, because the failure mode is silent and expensive.
#
# All four values below live in production as Cloudflare Worker secrets, set
# with `wrangler secret put`. That command is WRITE-ONLY: once a value is in
# Cloudflare there is no API, no dashboard, and no CLI that will ever show it
# to you again. If your only copy is the one you pasted into the prompt, then
# rotating it means minting a brand new one, a 401 cannot be told apart from a
# stray trailing newline, and a second Worker that later needs the same
# credential simply cannot have it.
#
# So: put the value HERE FIRST (in .env.local, which is gitignored), and only
# then push it to Cloudflare from the file. Never the other way around.
#
#   printf '%s' "$STEWARD_LAND_TOKEN" \
#     | npx wrangler secret put STEWARD_LAND_TOKEN --config wrangler.deploy.toml
#
# `printf`, never `echo`. echo appends a newline, the newline becomes part of
# the secret, and GitHub then rejects a token that looks perfect everywhere you
# inspect it. That bug costs an afternoon every single time.
#
# Record the mint date and expiry next to each token. A fine-grained PAT that
# quietly expires does NOT announce itself: the seat keeps deciding, logs a
# land failure, and carries on looking healthy. An unexplained "landing stopped
# working" is an expiry until proven otherwise.

# The commissioning bearer. Every /steward/:owner/:repo/* route requires it;
# without it the Worker answers 503 "seat not commissioned". Minted with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` — it is ours, not GitHub's, so it never expires.
# NOTE the PD_ prefix: this is the local/CLI name. The Worker secret is
# STEWARD_ADMIN_TOKEN. They are the same value under two names.
# PD_STEWARD_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# The tick's eyes. Read-only survey of PRs, checks and reviews. Absent ⇒ every
# wake logs "Tick held: cannot survey" and renders no verdicts. Fine-grained
# PAT, this repo only: Contents:Read, Pull requests:Read, Checks:Read.
# STEWARD_GITHUB_TOKEN=          # minted YYYY-MM-DD, expires YYYY-MM-DD

# The landing hand. PRESENCE OF THIS SECRET IS THE SWITCH — absent ⇒ every LAND
# verdict logs "seat holds no landing capability" and nothing is enqueued.
# A SEPARATE fine-grained PAT, this repo only: Contents:Read+Write and
# Pull requests:Read+Write, and NO admin or bypass rights.
#
# Non-admin is load-bearing, not hygiene: it is what makes GitHub itself refuse
# a landing whenever branch protection is unsatisfied, so the charter's "never
# land over a real red" is enforced by the platform rather than by the seat's
# good behavior. An admin token silently downgrades that guarantee to the
# honor system while looking identical in every log.
#
# To disarm landing without blinding the survey: revoke this token, or
# `wrangler secret delete STEWARD_LAND_TOKEN`. The seat keeps deciding and
# recording; it just stops acting.
# STEWARD_LAND_TOKEN=            # minted YYYY-MM-DD, expires YYYY-MM-DD

# SINGLE-TENANT TODAY. The two GitHub tokens above are one human's PATs, so the
# seat can only serve repos that human can write. Serving other people's repos
# needs per-installation tokens from the GitHub App (apps/relay/src/github-app.ts
# already mints them — getRepoInstallationId / getRepoToken), at which point
# both PATs become dead weight and should be deleted rather than left armed.
